{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b9e4cf9ce07ea8638f2c8986","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-8patuh"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"schema add-field accepts flag spellings the option parser splits or already owns implicitly, which can stop a command from starting"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported by an independent review of the option-collision change and not yet reproduced here. A custom field flag or alias containing a pipe is stored as one spelling, but the option parser splits a flag declaration at a pipe, so a flag such as full|detail registered for list tries to register a second full option and the command fails during registration, before its action runs and whatever flags the user typed. Separately, an alias equal to the short help flag is accepted because help is supplied implicitly and the existing-option test does not see it, after which the short help flag demands a value. Both are flag-spelling validation gaps that predate the collision check."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:cli","schema","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Reproduce both cases in a scratch tracker and record the observed failure; schema add-field, profile apply and rename-field refuse a flag or alias that is not exactly one option spelling, with a typed refusal naming the spelling; The implicit help flags are reserved for every command a field is registered for; validate reports stored definitions with such spellings"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-8jdc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A field flag that the parser would split or that shadows implicit help is refused at registration and reported by validate when already stored"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-pta8um","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"42fbe44d20e607373879f38e5278783fcdf3618a842feeedba4d958914f36cc2","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"24af42ebe187da075b8ba4455878aff86e8ef16524ae0e3740c49437dc0c024a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T21:43:15.467Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b9e4cf9ce07ea8638f2c8986","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T21:43:15.467Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-22T21:43:15.467Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Additional cases for this item from the second local review of PR 1768 (2026-11-22), none reproduced here yet:\n\n- rename-field accepts a target containing a comma and writes it as a flag, which the parser then splits; add-field already refuses commas.\n- An explicit short flag or alias equal to a built-in short option (for example the priority short flag) is accepted, after which registration skips it and the field has no usable spelling.\n- With a fields file that holds a duplicate key, a rename preview reads the hydrated definition while execution copies the first stored entry, so a preview can succeed where execution refuses after the plan was saved. The stage step does refuse; the preview should read the same entry.\n- A field whose key equals a global output control but whose flag is different (key json with another flag) is refused although the two flags work independently on the command line; decide whether a bare key should be compared only with options that reach the field reader.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"42fbe44d20e607373879f38e5278783fcdf3618a842feeedba4d958914f36cc2","after_hash":"04ea3391eb18654865d9fc1412f67324f0bc7921e8ca73908680e8fbd2a5c543","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"56159a843c36d21be3f3026d3bf50944f0e475a7a67a9cd5f04237910056237c"}
