{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:47:04.916Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3s4jwl+pm-8patuh+pm-g2zzus+pm-gh1769+pm-lulgxc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T08:47:04.913Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduced 2026-11-23 on 2026.11.23 in a scratch tracker before the fix: schema add-field detaily --commands list --alias 'full|deep' was stored, after which pm list -h failed during registration with \"Cannot add option '--full|deep <value>' to command 'list' due to conflicting flag '--full'\"; schema add-field helpz --commands search --alias=-h was stored and pm search foo -h then failed with 'Invalid command usage' because -h demanded a value; --alias=-p on create was accepted and silently skipped at registration (create -p still set priority); rename-field --to 'a,b' and 'a|b' were accepted.\n\nFix. src/core/schema/field-flag-spelling.ts (dependency-free, so CLI registration can consult it) defines one option spelling: a long name with no whitespace, pipe, comma, '=', or brackets, or a short flag of one dash and one character, following Commander 15.1's splitOptionFlags grammar. field-option-collisions.ts refuses defective spellings with schema_field_flag_invalid (add-field, profile apply, rename-field pre-plan and stage), compares a short spelling with the command's own short flags from the flag contracts (-p is --priority on create and update, free on list), and reserves the implicit --help/-h on every command. profile lint reports field_flag_invalid; validate --check-metadata reports stored spellings as validate_schema_field_flag_invalid with rows; addRuntimeFieldOption skips a defective stored spelling and the implicit help spellings, so a stored definition can no longer stop a command from starting or take over help (pm list --help and pm search -h now work beside such definitions).\n\nDecision on the comment's last bullet: a bare key equal to a global output control stays refused. The field reader looks the value up under the key as well as the flag, and which global options are stripped from command-scoped options is a separate list (extractCommandScopedOptions); tying the check to that list would let it drift, and the refusal only costs a rename. Not changed here: the rename preview reading the hydrated definition while staging copies the first stored entry of a duplicate key; the stage step already refuses, so execution stays correct.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:47:04.916Z"}],"before_hash":"7e5a3ef77d8cd66ce971fff7600d6c07feca7794247291f6d515dc759d5f78c7","after_hash":"db8fbde1ac06cc4d8ce5f6cb99988042b4cf5e22ae58423ec1aecea99a735766","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"04b59d719f3638a5ef9a417e045cb8c585e12bdcde3836d0c0cf8f873fd2d947"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:59:48.803Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3s4jwl+pm-8patuh+pm-g2zzus+pm-gh1769+pm-lulgxc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_edit","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/1/text","value":"Reproduced 2026-11-23 on 2026.11.23 in a scratch tracker before the fix: schema add-field detaily --commands list --alias 'full|deep' was stored, after which pm list -h failed during registration with \"Cannot add option '--full|deep <value>' to command 'list' due to conflicting flag '--full'\"; schema add-field helpz --commands search --alias=-h was stored and pm search foo -h then failed with 'Invalid command usage' because -h demanded a value; --alias=-p on create was accepted and silently skipped at registration (create -p still set priority); rename-field --to 'a,b' and 'a|b' were accepted.\n\nFix. src/sdk/schema/field-flag-spelling.ts (dependency-free, so CLI registration can consult it without a private core import) defines one option spelling: a long name with no whitespace, pipe, comma, '=', or brackets, or a short flag of one dash and one character, following Commander 15.1's splitOptionFlags grammar. field-option-collisions.ts refuses defective spellings with schema_field_flag_invalid (add-field, profile apply, rename-field pre-plan and stage), compares a short spelling with the command's own short flags from the flag contracts (-p is --priority on create and update, free on list), and reserves the implicit --help/-h on every command. profile lint reports field_flag_invalid; validate --check-metadata reports stored spellings as validate_schema_field_flag_invalid with rows; addRuntimeFieldOption skips a defective stored spelling and the implicit help spellings, so a stored definition can no longer stop a command from starting or take over help (pm list --help and pm search -h now work beside such definitions).\n\nDecision on the comment's last bullet: a bare key equal to a global output control stays refused. The field reader looks the value up under the key as well as the flag, and which global options are stripped from command-scoped options is a separate list (extractCommandScopedOptions); tying the check to that list would let it drift, and the refusal only costs a rename. Not changed here: the rename preview reading the hydrated definition while staging copies the first stored entry of a duplicate key; the stage step already refuses, so execution stays correct."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1/edited_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:59:48.802Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:59:48.803Z"}],"before_hash":"db8fbde1ac06cc4d8ce5f6cb99988042b4cf5e22ae58423ec1aecea99a735766","after_hash":"a9ec5df52cfa6fa488f220347a2b98758df265309aee6b11f64e5f36b1a1db23","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9b066f684e55cefe1c34f7de83367ea22ae711b6fbe90902010d4d4b00fe0bc3"}
